---
/** The landing page, in The Longest Journey's shape (SPEC §4.1): what the
 *  subject is, one button into the thing worth doing, the numbers on a
 *  hairline, and three short paragraphs with their sources under them.
 *
 *  Every number and date in the copy is computed from the knowledge base.
 *  None is typed in, so the page cannot disagree with the trace or the Act. */
import Base from '@layouts/Base.astro';
import { u } from '@lib/url';
import { SITE_NAME, kb, DATA_ACT_ELI } from '@lib/scope';
import { articles, rights, totals, trace, milestones } from '@lib/knowledge';
import { words, Words, times, day, month } from '@lib/format';

const A = await articles();
const R = await rights();
const T = await totals();
const TR = await trace();
const M = await milestones();
const C = T.composite, G = T.governed;

/* Stops inside the building: every hop before the one that crosses the
   property line. */
const inside = TR.hops.findIndex((h) => h.crosses_property_line);
const applies = M['application'].date;
const byDesign = M['data-by-design'].date;
const chargesEnd = M['switching-charges-end'].date;

/* The launch button appears when the trace does. Until phase 4 builds it the
   page says so instead of linking to nothing. */
const hasTrace = Object.keys(import.meta.glob('./trace/index.astro')).length > 0;
---
<Base title={SITE_NAME}>
  <div class="wrap section hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Connected buildings · EU Data Act</p>
    <h1 class="display" style="margin-top:.2em">{SITE_NAME}</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Every credential, every door event, every meter reading is a record of how a building works.
      One door event, followed from the front entrance to the cloud, is
      copied <span class="nw">{words(C.copies)} times.</span> Since {month(applies)} the EU Data Act
      has made that data the building owner’s to take and to move.
    </p>
    <div class="launch">
      {hasTrace ? (
        <a class="play plain" href={u('/trace/')}>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" width="15" height="15"><path d="M8 5.5v13l11-6.5z" fill="currentColor"/></svg>
          <span>Follow the data</span>
        </a>
      ) : (
        <span class="play waiting" aria-disabled="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" width="15" height="15"><path d="M8 5.5v13l11-6.5z" fill="currentColor"/></svg>
          <span>Follow the data</span>
        </span>
      )}
      <span class="ui muted">{hasTrace ? 'From the door to the cloud.' : 'The trace is being built.'}</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap">
    <hr class="rule" />
    <div class="stats">
      <div class="stat"><div class="eyebrow">Stops from the door</div><div class="value num">{T.hops}</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="eyebrow">Copies made</div><div class="value num">{C.copies}</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="eyebrow">Holders, many makers</div><div class="value num">{C.hands}</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="eyebrow">Holders, one maker</div><div class="value num">{G.hands}</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="eyebrow">Data Act articles</div><div class="value num">{A.length}</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="eyebrow">Rights for the owner</div><div class="value num">{R.length}</div></div>
    </div>
    <hr class="rule" />
  </div>

  <section class="wrap section more">
    <div class="three-up">
      <div>
        <h2 class="eyebrow">Where it goes</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          It starts at the reader on the front door. The controller logs it, the server in the comms room
          stores it, and the cloud keeps a replica and a backup. From there it can feed an AI model, or go
          to anyone the owner chooses. {Words(inside)} of its {words(T.hops)} stops are inside the building.
        </p>
        <p class="src">
          <a href={kb('building/the-trace')} rel="noopener">The trace</a> ·
          <a href={kb('building/the-building')} rel="noopener">The building</a>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="eyebrow">Who holds it</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          Every handoff copies the data. Built from several makers’ parts, the path leaves a copy with
          {words(C.hands)} companies and changes hands {times(C.seams)}. Run by one company, it leaves a
          copy with {words(G.hands)}, that company and its host, and changes hands {times(G.seams)}.
          Both make {words(C.copies)} copies.
        </p>
        <p class="src">
          <a href={kb('thesis/copies-and-hands')} rel="noopener">Copies and hands</a> ·
          <a href={kb('thesis/the-two-archetypes')} rel="noopener">The two archetypes</a> ·
          an illustrative system
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="eyebrow">What the owner is owed</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          In the EU the owner can take that data, free and machine-readable, and send it to any third
          party. Cloud contracts must say how to leave, and from <span class="nw">{day(chargesEnd)}</span>
          leaving costs nothing. Devices sold since <span class="nw">{day(byDesign)}</span> must be built
          so the data can be reached.
        </p>
        <p class="src">
          <a href={DATA_ACT_ELI} rel="noopener">Regulation (EU) 2023/2854</a>,
          Articles 3, 4, 5 and 29 ·
          <a href={kb('rights/yours')} rel="noopener">The rights</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  /* The whole page fits one laptop screen (about 830 px of browser height)
     without scrolling, as The Longest Journey's does: the spacing and the title
     scale with the window's height as well as its width, and give way first
     on a short one. */
  .hero { padding-block: clamp(20px, 3.6vh, 72px) clamp(24px, 3.4vh, 64px); }
  .hero .display { font-size: clamp(2.6rem, min(6vw, 8.6vh), var(--ks-type-display-size)); }
  .hero .lead { margin-top: clamp(.6em, 2vh, 1.2em); max-width: 50em; }
  .more { padding-block: clamp(20px, 3.4vh, 64px) clamp(6px, .8vh, 40px); }
  .launch { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: clamp(1rem, 3vh, 2rem) 0 0; }
  .play {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px;
    background: var(--ks-ink); color: var(--ks-paper);
    border-radius: var(--ks-radius-pill);
    padding: 10px 20px 10px 16px;
    font-size: var(--ks-type-ui-size); letter-spacing: .04em;
    transition: background var(--ks-quick) var(--ks-ease), transform var(--ks-quick) var(--ks-ease);
  }
  a.play:hover { background: var(--ks-instrument-raised); transform: translateY(-1px); }
  a.play:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--ks-patina-deep); outline-offset: 3px; }
  /* Until the trace exists the button is drawn, but as a promise rather than
     a control: no pointer, no hover, and the line beside it says why. */
  .play.waiting { background: var(--ks-gray-2); color: var(--ks-text-muted); cursor: default; }

  .stats { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(120px, 1fr)); gap: clamp(18px, 3vw, 40px); padding-block: clamp(16px, 2.6vh, 26px); }
  .stat .value { font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 1.6vw, var(--ks-type-title-lg-size)); font-weight: 300; color: var(--ks-ink); line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 2px; }
  .three-up { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(230px, 1fr)); gap: clamp(24px, 4vw, 48px); }
  .three-up .lead { margin-top: .7em; font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.55; }
  /* Sources sit under each paragraph rather than in it, so the three read as
     prose. */
  .src { margin: .7em 0 0; font-size: var(--ks-type-label-size); color: var(--ks-text-faint); }
  .src a { color: inherit; }
  .src a:hover { color: var(--ks-ink); }
  .lead { text-wrap: pretty; }
  .nw { white-space: nowrap; }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { a.play:hover { transform: none; } }
</style>
